    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a014df3_761424f5",
        "filename": "voltha/voltha.yml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000006
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-27T06:04:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest main config file entries reflecting subsystems within Voltha. So, for the first five entries, they are all for \"coordinator\", hence we shall use that as the entry name. Instead of \"Constants:\", lets use \"coordinator:\"\n\nIn fact, I suggest config values are nested to reflect the file path of the module where they are used, relative to voltha/voltha.\n\nAlso: please use snake_case entries in all config keys.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "999e47ee023dc758edef363386c29311e87cdcea",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a014df3_56f928c7",
        "filename": "voltha/voltha.yml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000006
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-27T06:04:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we drop the trailing slashes in all these five entry values (and make the code to add if needed)? It\u0027s cleaner that way.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "999e47ee023dc758edef363386c29311e87cdcea",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a014df3_36f69cd8",
        "filename": "voltha/voltha.yml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000006
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-27T06:04:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does not make too much sense this way. Why would anyone ever change FIVE_SEC to some other value than 5, or ONE_SEC to other than 1, etc.? What we want is to control the purpose. For instance, if in the code we currently hardcoded a foo action retry delay to 5, then the goal here is to make that configurable by lifting that into the config file with a\n\nfoo_action_retry_delay: 5\n\nentry. So we can change later to\n\nfoo_action_retry_delay: 10\n\netc.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "999e47ee023dc758edef363386c29311e87cdcea",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
